Q: Calculate multiple stats for two or more columns in R data.table A: <p>Make <code>stats()</code> return a list:</p>
<pre class="lang-r prettyprint-override"><code>stats &lt;- function(DT) {
    lapply(DT, \(x) c(maximo = max(x), minimo = min(x))) |&gt;
        unlist() |&gt;
        as.list()
}

dt[, stats(.SD), by = class, .SDcols = c('val1', 'val2')]

#    class val1.maximo val1.minimo val2.maximo val2.minimo
#    &lt;char&gt;       &lt;num&gt;       &lt;num&gt;       &lt;num&gt;       &lt;num&gt;
# 1:      a          12           4          90          10
# 2:      b           9           5         120          60
# 3:      c          11           1         100          30
</code></pre>
